# Build-time (public) variables — set in Cloudflare Pages → Settings → Environment variables.

# Plausible Analytics domain. Leave unset to disable analytics entirely.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN=doyel-labs.com

# Cloudflare Turnstile site key (client widget). The matching secret,
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY, is an encrypted Pages secret, never in this file.
NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=

# Server-side secrets (Pages Functions) — set as ENCRYPTED in the dashboard:
#   RESEND_API_KEY        sending-access scope only
#   TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY  server-side verify secret
# Plain-text function variables:
#   RESEND_FROM           e.g. "Doyel Labs Website <noreply@doyel-labs.com>"
#   CONTACT_TO            default support@doyel-labs.com
# Bindings (Pages → Settings → Functions):
#   RATE_LIMITER          Rate Limiting binding, 5 requests / 300 s (preferred)
#   CONTACT_KV            KV namespace (fallback if no Rate Limiting binding)
# In production (branch "master") the function refuses to run without a
# Turnstile secret and one rate-limit binding. See functions/api/contact.ts.
